---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="CLI Sentry and telemetry" activeNav="/cli/integrations/sentry">
  <h1>Sentry and telemetry</h1>
  <p>
    <code>appmctl sentry</code> manages the routed DSNs configured in the Web UI.
    <code>appmctl telemetry</code> reads grouped issues and distributed traces for one application.
    Both commands use the public API, so they are suitable for scripts and incident tooling.
  </p>

  <h2>Manage routed DSNs</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`appmctl sentry list
appmctl sentry get DSN_ID
appmctl sentry create --config sentry.json
appmctl sentry update DSN_ID --config sentry.json
appmctl sentry delete DSN_ID`} />
  <p>
    Create and update take a complete JSON configuration. This mirrors the Web UI form exactly and
    makes route replacement explicit. An update keeps the stored upstream secret when forwarding
    remains enabled and <code>upstream_dsn</code> is empty.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" code={`{
  "name": "Customer telemetry relay",
  "routing_method": "query",
  "event_source": null,
  "app_key": "app_slug",
  "identifier_key": "app_identifier",
  "target_mode": "selected",
  "blueprint_ids": [],
  "routes": [
    {
      "mobile_app_id": "019fc789-478f-71a0-9177-0ed28c77cff2",
      "app_identifier_id": "019fc789-478f-71a0-9177-0ed28c77cff3"
    }
  ],
  "forward_enabled": true,
  "upstream_dsn": "https://PUBLIC_KEY@sentry.example/PROJECT_ID",
  "enabled": true
}`} />
  <p>
    For event-metadata routing set <code>routing_method</code> to <code>event</code> and choose
    <code>event_source</code> from <code>auto</code>, <code>contexts</code>, <code>extra</code>,
    <code>tags</code>, or <code>attributes</code>. The API never returns the upstream DSN.
  </p>
  <p>
    Set <code>target_mode</code> to <code>all</code> for every current and future team application,
    <code>blueprints</code> with one or more <code>blueprint_ids</code> for a dynamic blueprint scope,
    or <code>selected</code> with explicit <code>routes</code>. An application-wide route accepts all
    identifiers and platforms attached to that application.
  </p>

  <h2>List issues and traces</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`appmctl --app customer-app telemetry issues
appmctl --app customer-app telemetry traces

# The filters match the Web UI
appmctl --app customer-app telemetry issues \
  --environment production \
  --identifier 019fc789-478f-71a0-9177-0ed28c77cff3 \
  --search checkout \
  --per-page 50`} />
  <p>
    An issue is the grouped error. Its individual arrivals are occurrences. A trace is keyed by the
    Sentry trace ID and can contain transaction events and errors from the same application.
  </p>

  <h2>Inspect a case</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`appmctl --json --app customer-app telemetry issue ISSUE_ID
appmctl --json --app customer-app telemetry issue ISSUE_ID --event OCCURRENCE_ID

appmctl --json --app customer-app telemetry trace TRACE_ID
appmctl --json --app customer-app telemetry trace TRACE_ID --event EVENT_ID`} />
  <p>
    Detail responses include the timeline and one complete selected event: exceptions and source
    context, request, user, contexts, tags, extra data, trace measurements, and untouched
    <code>raw_payload</code>. Use <code>--event</code> to move through the case without changing its ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Resolve or reopen an issue</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`appmctl --app customer-app telemetry resolve ISSUE_ID \
  --comment "Fixed in customer-web@1.4.1"
appmctl --app customer-app telemetry reopen ISSUE_ID \
  --comment "Regression reproduced in production"`} />
  <p>
    The comment is optional. Each status change records it together with the API key, its owner, and
    the time in the Issue and audit log. A later occurrence with the same fingerprint automatically
    reopens the issue as a system action, so a regression returns to the inbox.
  </p>

  <h2>Attach App Manager tags</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`appmctl --app customer-app telemetry tags ISSUE_ID \
  --tag 'production-regression:#f43f5e:heartbeat' \
  --tag checkout

appmctl --app customer-app telemetry tags ISSUE_ID --clear`} />
  <p>
    Repeat <code>--tag</code> to replace the Issue tag list. Its compact tuple syntax is
    <code>text[:#hex[:animation]]</code>; animations are <code>pulse</code>, <code>ping</code>,
    <code>flash</code>, <code>tada</code>, or <code>heartbeat</code>. These editable App Manager tags
    are separate from Sentry SDK tags, which stay unchanged on their original occurrences.
  </p>

  <h2>Scopes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>sentry list/get</code>: <code>integrations:read</code> and the team integration-management permission.</li>
    <li><code>sentry create/update/delete</code>: <code>integrations:write</code>.</li>
    <li><code>telemetry issues/issue/traces/trace</code>: <code>apps:read</code> and normal application view access.</li>
    <li><code>telemetry resolve/reopen/tags</code>: <code>apps:write</code> and application-management access.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The complete request and response schemas are also available in the <a href="/api-reference">API reference</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
